<h2 id="faq-heading">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="usa-accordion usa-accordion--bordered usa-accordion--multiselectable" data-allow-multiple="">
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="faq-1">What industries use packaging conveyors?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-1" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>Packaging conveyors serve food and beverage processing, pharmaceutical manufacturing, warehouse and distribution centers, automotive assembly, general manufacturing, and mining operations. Each industry requires different frame materials, sanitation ratings, speed ranges, and compliance certifications.</p>
<p><a href="/industries/food-conveyors/">Food-grade conveyors</a> require USDA acceptance, washdown ratings, and stainless steel construction. <a href="/industries/packaging-line-conveyors/">Packaging line conveyors</a> integrate with case packers, palletizers, and stretch wrappers. Pharmaceutical conveyors need cleanroom compatibility and GMP-validated controls.</p>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-2">How do conveyor requirements differ between industries?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-2" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p>The primary differences fall into five categories: material construction, environmental rating, regulatory compliance, speed/throughput, and load capacity.</p>
<ul>
<li><strong>Food &amp; Beverage:</strong> 304 or 316 stainless steel frames, FDA-compliant belts, IP65-IP69K washdown ratings, USDA/3-A acceptance</li>
<li><strong>Pharmaceutical:</strong> 316L stainless steel, particle-free designs, ISO Class 5-8 cleanroom compatible, cGMP validation</li>
<li><strong>Warehouse:</strong> Painted carbon steel, high-speed sortation, heavy case loads, PLC/WMS integration</li>
<li><strong>Automotive:</strong> Heavy structural steel, paint-line compatible coatings, high load capacity, overhead and inverted configurations</li>
</ul>

</div>
<h3 class="usa-accordion__heading"><button type="button" class="usa-accordion__button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="faq-3">What conveyor types work across multiple industries?</button></h3>
<div id="faq-3" class="usa-accordion__content usa-prose">
<p><a href="/conveyor-types/roller-conveyors/">Roller conveyors</a>, belt conveyors, and <a href="/conveyor-types/mdr-conveyors/">MDR conveyors</a> appear across nearly every industry. Manufacturers build these types in different material grades and configurations for each application.</p>
<p>For example, a roller conveyor for a warehouse uses galvanized steel rollers in a painted carbon steel frame. The same roller conveyor design for a food plant uses 304 stainless steel rollers in a fully welded stainless frame with sealed bearings and no exposed fasteners. Both use the same mechanical principles. The materials and finish standards differ.</p>

</div>
</div>
